<title>USA: Greyhound Lines stake cut by Toronto firm.</title>
<headline>Greyhound Lines stake cut by Toronto firm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Connor, Clark &amp; Co, an investment adviser based in Toronto, Ontario said Monday it cut its stake in Greyhound Lines Inc to 2,914,946 common shares or five percent from 6.1 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the company said it sold 588,434 common shares between January 7 and January 31 at prices ranging from $4.23 to $5.27 per share.</p>
<p>Greyhound Lines, based in Dallas, Texas, is a provider of intercity bus transportation services in the United States.</p>
</text>
